! The test re-cut road ~ test-first refactoring and the cap-stack lift

''What this carrier holds: train T's kit.'' The road holds the train's rows, rulings and order (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/the-order`>>); this kit holds what they rest on. The build order that makes the house's code testable at the grain its claims live at, ahead of the founding: a shared scratch fixture, events where tests poll, pure readers lifted out of the boot composer, instance-owned doors, the composer cut along capability lines into stages both vessel kinds share, and a mutation runner that scores what a test proves. Each row names what it builds, its red-first shape, the files it touches, what it waits on, and the house law it touches. Landed work reads in git and the CHANGELOG; a complete row moves to #/o-takiage at its land, and this carrier keeps only what stays owed.

''How it rides the house roadmap.'' The train runs ''beside'' the six paths of `stable-founding-road#/the-road`, never stalling them. The compose hunks of `open-node-vessel.ts` and `open-browser-vessel.ts` keep their named owners (`stable-founding-road` owner law): a row here reaches them only through a module boundary, or through the one named single-owner step `T12` holds.

''The lane law binds every lane here'' (`controller-handoff#/the-lane-law`, `mixed-model-swarm`): one lead per lane in its own worktree; red first, with a control; suites under a scratch `HOME` and a scratch `LAR_ROOT` with `LAR_BAGS` unset; never a boot in the tracked tree; canon lines in each commit, L-Prime kept.

''Train letter and rows.'' This train reads as ''T''. Its rows, their numbers and their statuses stand in the road's stride alone (#/the-rows), and this kit copies none: wave 0 holds the cures the cut reads found, and waves A to C the re-cut itself, and its lanes read `recut-<ground>`.

<<~/ahu>>

