<<~ ahu slot=`#/as-built`>>

!! The ground, measured 2026-10-31

|! Measure |! Reads |
| test to source, non-comment TS/MJS | 1.39 to 1 (204,872 test lines in 1,819 files); 1.08 to 1 raw, source running 39% comment lines |
| heaviest packages by ratio | `lararium-web` 2.02 · `lararium-node` 1.88 · `lararium-keyhive` 1.60 · `lararium-tw5` 1.50; node, mesh and tw5 carry 74% of test lines |
| where the weight comes from | repeated setup and breadth, never giant test files (p90 223 lines): 1,032 `mkdtemp` calls in 389 files; node runs 2.1 test files per source file |
| the god-method | `prepareNodeBootOn` (`open-node-vessel.ts`, about 709 to 3546): about 2,840 lines, 164 closures, 49 `let`s; 185 commits touched the file since 2026-10-01 |
| what blocks a small test | four process-global doors in `worker-handle.ts` (`setRestDoor`, `setCasDoor`, `setDyadDoor`, `setCustodyWriteDoor`): two vessels in one process overwrite each other's doors, so a test stands up nothing smaller than a whole boot; about 40 forward-declared cells tie the stages together |
| mutation testing | no Stryker config; a 14-mutant hand catalog for `lares-cli` (`tools/law-mutants-witness.sh`); fast-check rides the CLI laws suite alone. StrykerJS 10.1.0 (PR #6214, 2026-10-23) carries a vitest 5 fix tested against vitest 4.1.11; the repo pins vitest 5.0.3, so only the `T1` probe proves it here |
| dead exports | 53 names nothing references; 16 more ride barrel re-exports |
| flake families | the wiki-shore 2 s poll (`LandedLedger` fires no event) · the staged unlock answering before the store acknowledges · the TW5 dropdown e2e with no ready signal |

The scout reports behind this table rest outside the memegraph, in the controller's scratch: the two-wave scout, its cold refinement, and the god-method lift map.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-lift-map`>>

!! The god-method's lift map ~ sorted by capability

`prepareNodeBootOn` fuses two jobs. Its first half (R1 to R19) stands the cap-stack stages: the Repo, the face-gates, the share verdict, the membership, antigen and edge-shadow holders, the dials and the relays. Its second half (R22 to R35) builds the `VesselOrchestration` record (keel, wiki slot, daemon open, verb wiring, the pool, after-live). `composeCoreVessel` (`lararium-tw5/src/core-caps.ts`) already sequences that record for both vessel kinds, so the seam already stands.

The substrate: a vessel's host binding hands `composeCoreVessel` its ports; `openDaemonVmCore` starts the daemon island on a worker (`runSovereignKernel` → `TW5Engine.boot`), which holds the face-atom seed, Keyhive and the sealed store and asks its host for rest, cas, dyad and custody writes over its port. `VesselIslandPool` starts one worker per wiki. The browser vessel's worker runs the same kernel over IDB and OPFS. The page mirror boots one guarded engine with no syncer, fed by the port alone, and holds no truth.

Six lift targets, each row in #/the-rows naming its own:

# ''Inside the VM'': native TW5 cjs modules with a `module-type` header and tiddler metadata, compiled by the `plugin-build/` pipeline (46 modules ship so today), on the `*-vm` startup pattern where the host ships data in and the engine computes. Fits the verb-provider math and the wiki-act routing. Never transport, custody or keys. A shared-plugin module also loads in the glass mirror, so anything near custody rides a daemon-only plugin chosen by recipe.
# ''A pure module'', testable with no boot.
# ''A shared cap-stack stage'' in mesh or tw5, consumed by every vessel holding the capability; the browser twin burns in the same PR.
# ''A substrate adapter'' behind a narrow capability port: thread kind, store kind, socket server.
# ''A worker or process boundary.''
# ''Burning'': duplication a ruling already retired.

<<~/ahu>>

