<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-floor`>>

!! The floor ~ the forks the reads left, talked out

Operator, 2026-10-31: //"In this house, we 'talk story' to decide, we don't hold an invisible slot at the end of the turn for the operator ... Only surface things that survive this with uncertainty."// The house convened on the eight forks the reads named, two rounds each, against canon and a Gaia and an Elyncia story; every fork settled, and none survived to the operator.

```
<<~ talk-story slot=`#test-recut-forks` ground=`eight forks the cut reads left owed on this road` >>
bearings: forks parked as operator asks · each settled in-house against canon · the rows carry the settlement
telling: Council ranks the forks by what inherits shape; Stranger asks of each what capability it rests on;
Breach-Watch holds the security floor (verification never bends); Liminal checks none closes falsely.
Round one floated each house lean; round two pressed it with a story and the canon that governs.
<<~ moolelo held=`each fork below settles in-house; the rows carry it (house, under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-31)` >>
T5 daemonAuth: a node-local builder promoted later would stage "a now, b later"; the cut sorts by capability
  and browser vessels hold every cap. Settled: one pure shared builder in mesh, never surface-reachable,
  proven by a sentinel-seed no-leak test.
T5 boot pins: one relation, one name. Settled: node and browser pin one list under one reason tag.
T10: both readers agree. Settled: seven refuse-by-name cells; the share inputs keep a typed closed default with T11.
T11: the node verdict (`selfSlotShareDecision`) and the browser verdict (`federationShareDecision`, the relay-ring
  verdict) may answer different relations. Settled by measure, not by talk: the lane reads both first and lands
  ONE law per relation, capability-named; two laws stand only where a capability difference measures.
T12, T14: both readers agree. Settled as the rows read (pure deciders first; pure module before the VM step).
T13: Gaia, a teen's browser joins the household Nexus and later carries a sibling's wikis while the node sleeps;
  Elyncia, a district shrine's tablet stands the crossroads node's role when the orichalcum figure dims.
  Each needs the node's fuller behaviour in the browser. Settled: the five rows converge on node's form
  (several fleets with the roll read, face proof and plane registration, island resolution re-reading its pin
  per boot, founding and admit as one stage, the persona and face verbs shared by every vessel holding the cap).
T16/T20: the login suffix keys custody by an OS git email, a host fact; the house runs one operator per
  machine and container, and its second operator joins on her own machine. Shape-changing cuts land
  before she joins, under the alpha line. Settled: retire the suffix; custody resolves its home once at open.
  The cut re-names the operator's own custody files, a format cut the alpha line already sanctions.
T21: burning the one-use claim alone would leave a removed member re-entering on an old invite: a hole
  documented, never closed. Settled: the law stands as "a removed joiner never re-enters on an invite minted
  before the removal"; the red decides the mechanism (removal advancing the epoch, or a refusal keyed on the
  joiner's removal record), never a seen-cache that needs a shared registry.
<<~/moolelo >>
<<~/talk-story >>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-reads`>>

!! The reads behind the rows

The scouts and readers wrote to the controller's scratch, outside the memegraph, on 2026-10-31: the testability scout in two waves and its cold refinement; the god-method lift map; the root-map read; six cut reads by seam (pure readers, doors and cells, cap-stack stages, orchestration, browser twins, exports and homes) and a collision read beside each. What survived both waves stands in the rows above. Outside precedent they leaned on: fail-safe defaults (Saltzer and Schroeder), the new-enemy ordering in authorization systems (whose global timestamps the house's no-global-now law declines; refresh-then-drop inside the serial refold chain stands as the house analogue), characterization tests before extraction (Feathers), named exemptions for held seats in dead-code tools, TiddlyWiki's own boot sequencing (read whole), and the Automerge Repo share configuration. Most sources stood at search-summary level; each row's red decides, never the citation.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/laws`>>

!! The laws each row keeps

* ''Red first, with a control'' (`working-procedures#/red-first`): mutation kill data never deletes a control, which by design kills no unique mutant.
* ''No key on a surface'': no custody, transport or key path lifts into a shared-plugin module the mirror loads.
* ''Custody and identity read by capability, never by host'': every stage and port carries a capability name.
* ''One owner per registry'': the process-global doors break it per process, and `T9` cures it.
* ''No global now'': fake timers patch the global clock (23 test files use them today), so a new seam waits on an event or an injected clock, never a patched global.
* ''Web3 only'': the Stryker dashboard never enters the stack; local reporters only.
* ''Old shapes burn'': each cut lands whole, with no shim beside it.

<<~/ahu>>

